{number: 8}
{title: Come, Thou Fount of Every Blessing}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[D] Come, Thou Fount of [A] every blessing, [G] tune my [A] heart to [D] sing Thy grace;
[D] Streams of mercy, [A] never ceasing, [G] call for [A] songs of [D] loudest praise.
Teach me [F#m] some me-[G] lodious [D] sonnet, [A] sung by [F#m] flaming [G] tongues a-[A] bove;
[D] Praise the mount! I’m [A] fixed upon it, [G] mount of [A] Thy redeeming [D] love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[D] Here I raise mine [A] Ebenezer; [G] hither [A] by Thy [D] help I’m come;
[D] And I hope, by [A] Thy good pleasure, [G] safely [A] to ar-[D] rive at home.
Jesus [F#m] sought me [G] when a [D] stranger, [A] wandering [F#m] from the [G] fold of [A] God;
[D] He, to rescue [A] me from danger, [G] inter-[A] posed His precious [D] blood.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[D] O to grace how [A] great a debtor [G] daily [A] I’m con-[D] strained to be!
[D] Let Thy goodness, [A] like a fetter, [G] bind my [A] wandering [D] heart to Thee:
Prone to [F#m] wander, [G] Lord, I [D] feel it, [A] prone to [F#m] leave the [G] God I [A] love;
[D] Here’s my heart, O [A] take and seal it, [G] seal it [A] for Thy courts a-[D] bove.
{end_of_verse}
